                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "227602257",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199000690122",
                            "num_reviews": 35,
                            "playtime_forever": 24,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 24,
                            "last_played": 1781047033
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I went into this expecting an improved version of the original Music Racer, but I was honestly shocked by how unfinished it feels. The biggest issue is that local tracks often won't load at all. When it happens, the game completely breaks and becomes unplayable, forcing you to restart multiple times just to get back to normal gameplay.\r\n\r\nEven when it works, the song volume is far too low, which hurts the core experience of a music-based game. It's especially disappointing because there are some genuinely good new ideas here, and I can see the potential. Unfortunately, the game feels rushed and lacks the polish it needed before release.\r\n\r\nI would love to see the developer focus on bug fixes and stability updates, because there is a solid foundation underneath the issues IF they ever come back.. but for now, I'd recommend sticking with the original Music Racer and saving your $0.99. In its current state, this version isn't worth the money and you ARE wasting your TIME and money.\r\n",
